865	    /**
866	     * Rejects the request when the incoming owner's derived {@code identityKey} exactly matches that
867	     * of any existing owner. The key (the SHA-256 hex digest of {@code normalizedTelephone + '|' +
868	     * lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)}) is the single consolidated duplicate-detection key that
869	     * replaces the former separate telephone, email and household checks. Because the telephone is
870	     * part of the key, two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones have
871	     * different keys and are both allowed (they surface as a soft match instead); only an exact
872	     * full-key match is a duplicate. Soft-deleted owners are ignored, and the email-domain blocklist
873	     * has already been applied when the email was normalized. The key is derived identically for the
874	     * incoming and existing owners via {@link OwnerMapper#toIdentityKey}.
